# Kubernetes-cluster variant of deploy/caddy/Caddyfile — same routing rules,
# same upstream role names (api:8000, web:8080 resolve as plain Kubernetes
# Service DNS names within the ghostrange namespace, same as they resolved as
# docker-compose service names on the Compute VM).
#
# DIFFERENCE FROM deploy/caddy/Caddyfile: the Compute-VM Caddyfile hardcodes the
# VM's known-in-advance public IP (45.76.248.45.nip.io / .sslip.io) as the site
# address so Caddy can request a Let's Encrypt cert for it immediately. On VKE,
# the public IP is a Vultr Load Balancer IP that is NOT known until after this
# Service is created (see docs/deployment/VKE_DEPLOY.md step 5). This base
# Caddyfile therefore serves plain HTTP on any Host (`:80` catch-all, no TLS)
# so it deploys and routes correctly from minute one; the runbook's post-deploy
# step swaps this ConfigMap to the real `<lb-ip>.sslip.io, :443 { tls ... }`
# form once the LB IP exists, then rolls the caddy Deployment — the same
# one-time "insert the real IP" edit this repo already does today for the
# Compute VM, not new complexity.
{
	admin off
}

:80 {
	encode gzip

	handle /api/* {
		uri strip_prefix /api
		reverse_proxy api:8000 {
			flush_interval -1
		}
	}

	handle /v1/* {
		reverse_proxy api:8000 {
			flush_interval -1
		}
	}

	handle /health* {
		reverse_proxy api:8000
	}

	handle {
		reverse_proxy web:8080
	}
}
